+// engine-patches/0414: the MTLDevice path's pipeline archive (DM_PSO_BINARY_ARCHIVE), on this Mac's GPU with DM_PSO_MTL4=0 (the path iOS takes) and pipelines from a library compiled from
+// source at run time. Each scenario is a process of its own (this binary run again), as a session on the phone is. What it shows:
+//  - a session that ends by quitting (mtl_arch_save's end, atexit's), by SIGTERM's graceful exit (which ends with _exit), or by going to the background (dm_gfx_suspend(1)) and then
+//    SIGKILL (jetsam, or iOS ending a suspended app) writes the archive, and the NEXT process takes every render, compute and mesh pipeline from it (FailOnBinaryArchiveMiss), and builds
+//    one it never saw;
+//  - heat holds adds back instead of dropping them: none at Critical or with little memory, DVA_HOT_BATCH a tick at Serious, the rest once cool; at most DVA_PENDING_MAX wait;
+//  - a failed write does not turn the archive off: it goes on from its last written file (what was added since is lost, what was written is still found), off after DVA_FAIL_MAX;
+//  - a file made for another host build / chain / OS / GPU is dropped, an unreadable one started again, and the Metal 4 path (DM_PSO_MTL4=1) does not use it.
